// Change: update to existing rule
// Title: DLL Search Order Hijackig Via Additional Space in Path
// Sigma ID: b6f91281-20aa-446a-b986-38a92813a18f
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: frack113, Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-07-30 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: persistence, privilege-escalation, execution, stealth, T1574.001
// Description: Detects when an attacker create a similar folder structure to windows system folders such as
//   (Windows, Program Files...) but with a space in order to trick DLL load search order and perform
//   a "DLL Search Order Hijacking" attack
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/cyb3rops/status/1552932770464292864
//   - https://www.wietzebeukema.nl/blog/hijacking-dlls-in-windows
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ad147b5514596e70f2782769d9833046b7c8e12b/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_dll_sideloading_space_path.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where (FolderPath startswith "C:\\Windows \\" or FolderPath startswith "C:\\Program Files \\" or FolderPath startswith "C:\\Program Files (x86) \\") and FolderPath endswith ".dll"
